# Operator-machine secrets for the Wave 5 Q2 8h oracle-refresh cron.
#
# Copy to `refresh-and-ingest.env` (gitignored) and fill in the placeholders.
# Source of truth for both secrets is the backend's `.env` on the homelab:
#   ssh ... cat /home/muhaven/Project/Fhenix/MuHaven/backend/.env \
#     | grep -E 'ORACLE_INGEST_SERVICE_SECRET|OPERATOR_ALERT_TEST_SECRET'
#
# Security notes:
# - `scripts/refresh-and-ingest.sh` sources this file as shell-locals (NOT
#   `set -a`) so neither secret leaks into the env of `npm run refresh:all`.
#   The ingest secret is passed to the ingest phase via inline-prefix; the
#   alert secret never leaves the wrapper process.
# - Per-run logs are created with `umask 077` so other Windows users can't
#   read them. The wrapper also strips control characters from the alert
#   note before posting.
# - Filling secrets with their literal placeholder (`<<FILL>>`) is detected
#   and rejected by the wrapper -- a half-edited file fails CONFIG, not at
#   first 401.

# Required. Quote the placeholder so bash's heredoc operator (`<<`) doesn't
# eat the line at source time -- the wrapper sources this file via `.` so
# any unquoted shell metacharacter would break before validation runs.
ORACLE_INGEST_SERVICE_SECRET='<<FILL>>'
OPERATOR_ALERT_TEST_SECRET='<<FILL>>'

# Optional -- defaults shown
# ORACLE_INGEST_URL=https://api.muhaven.app
# OPERATOR_ALERT_URL=https://api.muhaven.app
# LOG_RETENTION_RUNS=30
